    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96382" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέγ-ασμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>anything which covers</i> or <i>shelters, covering</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				1.5.10
			</span></i> (pl.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τεύτλου κρύπτεται στεγάσμασιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					181
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. ὤας ἢ διφθέρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					1259.5
				</span></i>
			 (Athens, <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ς. τοῖς πλοίοις</span>”
				<i>awnings,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					PCair.Zen.
					53.7
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>roof</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκέπασμα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				279d
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Criti.</u>
				111c
			</span></i>.</div>
